      "round_summary": "Round 2/3 (retry): Fix assertion type mismatch for `final_state_reachable_within_30_cycles`. `fvCover` not available in this Chisel-FV version — use standard Chisel `cover()` primitive instead. The `astRelaxedLiveness` macro implements a universal bounded-liveness property (all valid paths must reach `io.finalState` within 30 cycles), but the intended verification goal is existential reachability. Even with round-1 assumptions, the solver can always select NONE after one move (moving goat right, then doing nothing) and never reach the final state — causing universal assertion to always fail. Fix: replace `astRelaxedLiveness` with a bounded timer + `cover(io.finalState && pending, \"final_state_reachable_within_30_cycles\")` which asks the formal tool whether `io.finalState` is reachable within 30 cycles under the assumptions. The assertion label `final_state_reachable_within_30_cycles` is preserved exactly as the cover label. No homologous assertions to repair. All other assertions unchanged.",
